    <string name="ubuntu_consent_title">Ubuntu needs to be downloaded</string>
    <string name="ubuntu_consent_body">ThothTerm Resolute runs a real Ubuntu %1$s userland. This build does not include it, so it has to be downloaded before the terminal can start.\n\nWhat will be downloaded:\n\u2022 Now: the Ubuntu %1$s base system, about %2$d MB, from %3$s.\n\u2022 Right after, in the background: Ubuntu\u2019s package lists and the sudo package, about 30 MB (it varies as the archive changes), from Ubuntu\u2019s package archive, archive.ubuntu.com and security.ubuntu.com. The terminal opens without waiting for this step; if it fails, the terminal still works and the menu offers to retry it.\n\nWhat you are agreeing to:\n\u2022 This downloads executable software onto your device after installation.\n\u2022 That software is published by Canonical, not by ThothTerm.\n\u2022 It is not part of this app\u2019s package and was not built or verified by F\u2011Droid.\n\u2022 ThothTerm checks the base system against a SHA\u2011256 checksum that is fixed in this app\u2019s source, and refuses it if it does not match. apt checks the packages against Ubuntu\u2019s archive signing keys.\n\nNothing is downloaded unless you choose Download Ubuntu. Later, the app contacts the package archive only when sudo is missing (a setup that failed, or you removed it) to install it again; any other download is apt run by you.</string>
