    <string name="service_special_use" translatable="false">
        My application, ThothTerm, opens "terminal" windows with command-line interpreter(born shell).
        In a window, the user can execute a command such as secure shell (ssh), which allows them to connect to their servers remotely.
        Remark: Secure shell replaces insecure protocols like rlogin and is preferred by users for its robust encryption, strong authentication, and data integrity.
        It enables remote command execution(SSH), file transfers (SFTP/SCP) in a secure network connection over reliable protocol(TCP).
        When is opened a terminal users expects session to remain active even when application is minimised.
        One of reasons is long-running tasks like command execution, data transfers, software compilation, many administrative tasks.
        The user does not want an abrupt termination of the session because it may disrupt ongoing processes.
        Termination may cause data loss, may leave orphaned jobs, or may require manual cleanup and so frustrate and disappoint users.
        Commands like ssh keep-alive prevent idle timeouts, ensuring an active connection, and avoiding disconnection due to inactivity.
        While the application is running, it provides a clear notification to users that a terminal session is running.
        The use of "Foreground Service" is critical to maintain sessions.
        It is essential to deliver reliable, and uninterrupted session that application users rely on, and that ensures a seamless user experience.
        The application request only necessary permissions and this texts provides detailed information on data usage.
    </string>
